/*!
\page page_sttrigger StTrigger

\brief Base class for STAR trigger information; stores the trigger word and action word.

\section sttrigger_overview Overview
\c StTrigger is the base class for all STAR trigger objects (\ref page_stl0trigger,
\ref page_stl1trigger).  It stores the two words common to every trigger level:
the L0 hardware trigger word (which conditions fired) and the trigger action word
(which detector/algorithm responses were invoked).  Subclasses extend it with
level-specific data.

\section sttrigger_hierarchy Class Hierarchy
\code
TObject
 └── StObject
      └── StTrigger
           ├── StL0Trigger
           └── StL1Trigger
\endcode

\section sttrigger_members Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| UInt_t | mTriggerWord | L0 hardware trigger word |
| UInt_t | mTriggerActionWord | Trigger action word |

\section sttrigger_methods Key Methods

| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| `unsigned int triggerWord() const` | L0 hardware trigger word |
| `unsigned int triggerActionWord() const` | Trigger action word |
| `void setTriggerWord(unsigned int)` | Set trigger word |
| `void setTriggerActionWord(unsigned int)` | Set action word |

\section sttrigger_usage Usage Example
\code{.cpp}
StL0Trigger* l0 = event->l0Trigger();
if (l0)
    cout << "Trigger word: 0x" << hex << l0->triggerWord() << endl;
\endcode

\see \ref page_stl0trigger
\see \ref page_stl1trigger
\see \ref page_stl3trigger
*/
